<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45448" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφύλακτος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to keep</i> or <i>guard</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				998
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἡ καρδία</span>
			<i>well-guarded</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				670a26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφυλακτότερον τὸ ὕδωρ τοῦ
				ἀέρος</span>
			<i>more easily confined</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				438a15
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				656b2
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν εὐφυλάκτῳ
			εἶναι</span> to be <i>on one's guard</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				201
			</span></i>; -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερα αὐτοῖς ἐγίγνετο</span>
			it was <i>easier</i> for them <i>to keep a look-out</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.55
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπως εὐφύλακτα αὐτοῖς εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.92
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλάττομαι</span>) <i>easy to guard against</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>SE</u>
				174b35
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				57.1
			</span></i>.</div>
